<BaseLayout title='About | Trouvus' description='Trouvus closes the gap between AI possibility and organizational reality through research-grounded transformation.'>
<section class="page-hero"><canvas class="hero-canvas" data-variant="network"></canvas><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">About Trouvus</div><h1>Closing the gap between AI possibility and organizational reality.</h1><p class="lead">Trouvus integrates research, strategy, organizational design and implementation discipline to help leaders make consequential technology decisions.</p></div></section><section><div class="wrap split"><div><h2>Where research meets implementation.</h2></div><div><p class="lead">Trouvus was founded by Dr. Mitt Nowshade Kabir to translate advances in AI, digital transformation and technology management into practical business-model, operating-model and workforce decisions.</p><p>The current enterprise AI focus builds on an earlier history of Trouvus client advisory work, alongside management scholarship, entrepreneurship and executive education. This multidisciplinary foundation enables Trouvus to examine not only whether a technology works, but where it creates value, how it changes work and what organizational capabilities are required to sustain it.</p></div></div></section><section class="rule"><div class="wrap split"><div><div class="eyebrow">Founder</div><h2>Dr. Mitt Nowshade Kabir</h2></div><div><p class="lead">An AI and digital-transformation strategist, serial entrepreneur and academic with more than three decades of experience at the intersection of emerging technology, innovation and business strategy.</p><p>Dr. Kabir holds a Ph.D. in Information Technology, a Doctorate in Business Administration, an M.Sc. in Computer Science and an MBA. He is the author of <a class="source-link" href="https://link.springer.com/book/10.1057/978-1-137-34809-8" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><em>Knowledge-Based Social Entrepreneurship</em></a> (Palgrave Macmillan) and has published more than thirty peer-reviewed research papers spanning AI strategy, generative-AI governance, human-AI co-creation, knowledge management and digital transformation.</p><p>He has served as an Adjunct Professor of Digital Transformation, chaired the European Conference on the Impact of Artificial Intelligence and Robotics (ECIAIR), and advised governments, boards and businesses on advanced technologies, business development and innovation strategy. As an entrepreneur he has founded and built technology ventures in e-commerce and enterprise software across international markets.</p><div class="grid-2"><div class="card"><h3>Research</h3><p class="muted">30+ peer-reviewed papers; author, <em>Knowledge-Based Social Entrepreneurship</em> (Palgrave Macmillan).</p></div><div class="card"><h3>Teaching</h3><p class="muted">Adjunct Professor of Digital Transformation; executive education for leadership teams.</p></div><div class="card"><h3>Academic leadership</h3><p class="muted">Programme Chair, European Conference on the Impact of AI and Robotics (ECIAIR).</p></div><div class="card"><h3>Practice</h3><p class="muted">Serial technology entrepreneur; advisor to governments, boards and growth businesses.</p></div></div></div></div></section><section class="rule"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">Operating principles</div><div class="grid-3"><div class="card"><img class="icon" loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="/images/icon-evidence.svg" alt=""><h3>Evidence before enthusiasm</h3><p class="muted">We distinguish demonstrated capability, informed inference and unproven promise.</p></div><div class="card"><img class="icon" loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="/images/icon-strategy.svg" alt=""><h3>Strategy before technology</h3><p class="muted">We start with the decision, value logic and operating context.</p></div><div class="card"><img class="icon" loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="/images/icon-workforce.svg" alt=""><h3>Capability before scale</h3><p class="muted">Transformation becomes durable when ownership and competence exist inside the organization.</p></div><div class="card"><img class="icon" loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="/images/icon-bizmodel.svg" alt=""><h3>Human agency alongside automation</h3><p class="muted">Critical judgment and adaptive capacity must remain load-bearing organizational assets.</p></div><div class="card"><img class="icon" loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="/images/icon-implementation.svg" alt=""><h3>Measurable outcomes over activity</h3><p class="muted">Workshops, pilots and systems are means; business and organizational outcomes are the test.</p></div><div class="card"><img class="icon" loading="lazy" decoding="async" src="/images/icon-diagnose.svg" alt=""><h3>Responsible transformation by design</h3><p class="muted">Governance, risk and accountability should be built into the operating model.</p></div></div></div></section><section><div class="wrap"><div class="quote">“AI transformation succeeds when strategy, operating processes, technology, governance and human capability are redesigned together.”</div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
